        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "We seeded three items: keyboard, dock, and arm. The local service is running, but the list looks short."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "Local inventory service",
      "visualBeat": "Terminal shows npm run demo; browser list displays only two items.",
      "factIds": [
        "c3",
        "c4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-1",
      "turns": [
        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "I checked the code. The service projects the Products entity and marks it readonly. That explains why I cannot create new items."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "Entity is readonly",
      "visualBeat": "Cursor hovers over @readonly annotation; a create request icon turns red.",
      "factIds": [
        "c2",
        "c5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-2",
      "turns": [
        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "But readonly does not hide existing rows. I added a filter: stock greater than zero. Suddenly, the arm disappeared again."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "Filter: stock > 0",
      "visualBeat": "Filter bar updates; monitor arm card slides away, leaving keyboard and dock.",
      "factIds": [
        "c5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-3",
      "turns": [
        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "Wait. The arm has zero stock. The filter is doing its job. It is not a bug; it is a business rule."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "Zero stock logic",
      "visualBeat": "Zoom into monitor arm card showing stock: 0; a checkmark appears.",
      "factIds": [
        "c4",
        "c5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "payoff",
      "turns": [
        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "Remove the filter, and all three return. The service is healthy. Your data model controls what the API sees."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "All rows returned",
      "visualBeat": "Filter removed; all three product cards reappear in the list.",
      "factIds": [
        "c5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cta",
      "turns": [
        {
          "speakerId": "narrator",
          "text": "Check your filters next. This is a local prototype; production auth is separate work. Try it in your CAP project."
        }
      ],
      "screenText": "Try it locally",
      "visualBeat": "Narrator points to a local terminal prompt; text overlay notes prototype scope.",
      "factIds": [
        "c6"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "editorNotes": "The 'missing service' failure from fact c6 is not demonstrated in this draft; only the filter behavior is shown. The readonly rejection is mentioned but not visually detailed as a 405 error screen to keep the story focused on the filter reveal."
}

